{
  "id": "Compound::DB00477 - Gene::1128",
  "verbalization": "Chlorpromazine is implicated in the interaction with Hrh4, which participates in multiple receptor-related activities, including G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity and neuro transmitter receptor activity. These pathways are central to the function of Chrm1, a receptor involved in neurotransmission. The evidence suggests that Chlorpromazine may modulate Chrm1 through a mechanism involving Hrh4, which acts as a bridge between the drug and the receptor. The overlapping participation of Hrh4 in different receptor activities indicates a potential role in the regulation of Chrm1 function. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Chlorpromazine influences Chrm1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
